  "description": "A scene depicting a cemetery with tombstones under a cloudy sky, overlaid with text that reads: 'if you're not grilling at my grave site we were never really friends.' The scene uses a darkly humorous and morbid analogy to express a sense of finality or betrayal in a friendship. The humor is derived from the juxtaposition of a solemn, final setting (a cemetery) with a casual, social activity (grilling), creating a jarring and potentially offensive contrast.",
